            <ArticleTitle>Repair of posterolateral ventral herniation caused by diabetic truncal neuropathy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>703-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Abdominal pain caused by diabetic radiculopathy is uncommon, and abdominal hernia as a complication is rare. We report a case of abdominal wall herniation caused by diabetic truncal radiculopathy requiring surgical repair. Clinical and diagnostic features of this entity are reviewed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
